{"id": "npmountrainier", "name": "Mount Rainier National Park", "short": "Mount Rainier", "place": "Washington, USA", "lat": 46.85, "lon": -121.75, "side": "l", "cont": "North America", "country": "United States of America", "states": ["Washington"], "kind": "Polar & mountain", "park": true, "blurb": "Old-growth forest, flower meadows and cliffs where marmots, goats and cougars live.", "tip": {"id": "cougar", "title": "Remove the cougar", "text": "Cougars hunt deer, elk and mountain goats. Set Cougar to -100% and watch those herbivores, then the meadow plants and berries they eat."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Mount Rainier National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Rainier_National_Park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Hoary marmot", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hoary_marmot"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Mountain goat", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_goat"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: American pika", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_pika"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Cougar", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cougar"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Douglas squirrel", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Douglas_squirrel"}], "notes": "The story and why it matters come from the Wikipedia articles listed below (Mount Rainier National Park, Hoary marmot, Mountain goat). Individual species and links have not been checked one by one. Feeding links that match a GloBI (Global Biotic Interactions) record are marked in the node details, with a link to the records. A few links were added from GloBI records.", "imgwiki": "Mount Rainier National Park", "icon": "whitebark", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "rain", "sp": "rain", "xh": 0.08}, {"id": "snow", "sp": "snowpack & glaciers", "xh": 0.28}, {"id": "sun", "sp": "short summer sun", "xh": 0.48}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "volcanic mountain soil", "xh": 0.68}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposer community", "xh": 0.9, "name": "Fungi & soil microbes", "desc": "Break down fallen logs, needles and carcasses and return nutrients to the soil."}, {"id": "hemlock", "sp": "tsuga heterophylla", "xh": 0.12, "badge": "Foundation species"}, {"id": "fir", "sp": "abies lasiocarpa", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "lily", "sp": "erythronium montanum", "xh": 0.5}, {"id": "fireweed", "sp": "chamaenerion angustifolium", "xh": 0.7, "desc": "A tall wildflower of clearings and meadows. Deer, pikas and bumble bees feed on it, according to records and Wikipedia."}, {"id": "huckle", "sp": "vaccinium membranaceum", "xh": 0.88}, {"id": "marmot", "sp": "marmota caligata", "xh": 0.04, "desc": "A big ground squirrel of rocky alpine meadows. Wikipedia says it eats leaves, flowers, grasses and sedges."}, {"id": "pika", "sp": "ochotona princeps", "xh": 0.17, "desc": "A small relative of rabbits living in rock slides. Eats grasses, sedges and fireweed, and stacks hay piles for winter."}, {"id": "goat", "sp": "oreamnos americanus", "xh": 0.3, "desc": "Grazes grasses, herbs, sedges and low shrubs on steep slopes. Cougars are its main predator, and cliffs are its best defence."}, {"id": "deer", "sp": "odocoileus hemionus", "xh": 0.43, "wiki": "Mule deer", "desc": "Browses shrubs and herbs, including fireweed. A staple prey of cougars."}, {"id": "elk", "sp": "cervus canadensis", "xh": 0.56, "desc": "A large grazer and browser of forest and meadow. Recorded in GBIF data under the name red deer."}, {"id": "dsquirrel", "sp": "tamiasciurus douglasii", "xh": 0.69, "desc": "Eats mostly conifer seeds and stores cones in a midden. Also eats fungi and berries."}, {"id": "vole", "sp": "myodes gapperi", "xh": 0.82, "name": "Gapper's red-backed vole", "wiki": "Southern red-backed vole", "desc": "A small rodent of the forest floor, eaten by foxes, hawks and bears in GloBI records.", "ic": "vole"}, {"id": "bear", "sp": "ursus americanus", "xh": 0.12, "name": "American black bear", "tl": 3, "wiki": "American black bear", "desc": "An omnivore that eats berries, plants, small mammals and deer or elk. Often takes over carcasses left by cougars."}, {"id": "fox", "sp": "vulpes vulpes", "xh": 0.34, "desc": "Hunts voles, mice and small mammals and eats carrion. GloBI also lists deer and birds among its food."}, {"id": "hawk", "sp": "buteo jamaicensis", "xh": 0.58, "tl": 3, "wiki": "Red-tailed hawk", "desc": "A hawk that hunts small mammals such as voles and also snakes and birds.", "ic": "hawk"}, {"id": "raven", "sp": "corvus corax", "xh": 0.8, "desc": "A clever scavenger that feeds on carcasses along with small prey and scraps."}, {"id": "cougar", "sp": "puma concolor", "xh": 0.3, "name": "Cougar", "desc": "The mountain lion hunts mainly deer and elk, and also goats. Bears often take over its kills.", "badge": "Keystone predator"}, {"id": "goldeneagle", "sp": "aquila chrysaetos", "xh": 0.66, "desc": "An eagle of open alpine ground that preys on marmots, pikas and other mammals."}], "raw": [["rain", "hemlock", "r"], ["rain", "fir", "r"], ["rain", "huckle", "r"], ["snow", "fir", "r"], ["snow", "lily", "r"], ["sun", "lily", "r"], ["sun", "fireweed", "r"], ["sun", "huckle", "r"], ["soil", "hemlock", "r"], ["soil", "fir", "r"], ["soil", "huckle", "r"], ["decomp", "soil", "r"], ["hemlock", "dsquirrel"], ["fir", "dsquirrel"], ["fir", "goat"], ["lily", "marmot"], ["lily", "goat"], ["lily", "elk"], ["fireweed", "pika"], ["fireweed", "deer"], ["huckle", "bear"], ["huckle", "deer"], ["huckle", "elk"], ["huckle", "dsquirrel"], ["huckle", "vole"], ["marmot", "goldeneagle"], ["marmot", "bear"], ["marmot", "fox"], ["marmot", "cougar"], ["pika", "goldeneagle"], ["pika", "hawk"], ["pika", "fox"], ["goat", "cougar"], ["deer", "cougar"], ["elk", "cougar"], ["deer", "bear"], ["elk", "bear"], ["vole", "bear"], ["vole", "fox"], ["vole", "hawk"], ["deer", "fox", "s"], ["deer", "raven", "s"], ["elk", "raven", "s"], ["vole", "raven"], ["hemlock", "decomp", "d"], ["fir", "decomp", "d"], ["lily", "decomp", "d"], ["deer", "decomp", "d"], ["elk", "decomp", "d"], ["hemlock", "deer"], ["goat", "bear"], ["deer", "hawk"], ["dsquirrel", "raven"], ["bear", "cougar"], ["fox", "cougar"], ["goat", "goldeneagle"], ["deer", "goldeneagle"], ["elk", "goldeneagle"], ["fox", "goldeneagle"], ["hawk", "goldeneagle"], ["raven", "goldeneagle"]], "ev": {"hemlock>dsquirrel": ["a"], "fir>dsquirrel": ["gg", "Tamiasciurus douglasii", "Abies lasiocarpa"], "fir>goat": ["a"], "lily>marmot": ["a"], "lily>goat": ["a"], "lily>elk": ["a"], "fireweed>pika": ["a"], "fireweed>deer": ["g", "Odocoileus hemionus", "Chamaenerion angustifolium"], "huckle>bear": ["gg", "Ursus americanus", "Vaccinium membranaceum"], "huckle>deer": ["gg", "Odocoileus hemionus", "Vaccinium membranaceum"], "huckle>elk": ["a"], "huckle>dsquirrel": ["a"], "huckle>vole": ["gg", "Myodes gapperi", "Vaccinium membranaceum"], "marmot>goldeneagle": ["gg", "Aquila chrysaetos", "Marmota caligata"], "marmot>bear": ["gg", "Ursus americanus", "Marmota caligata"], "marmot>fox": ["gg", "Vulpes vulpes", "Marmota caligata"], "marmot>cougar": ["gg", "Puma concolor", "Marmota caligata"], "pika>goldeneagle": ["gg", "Aquila chrysaetos", "Ochotona princeps"], "pika>hawk": ["a"], "pika>fox": ["gg", "Vulpes vulpes", "Ochotona princeps"], "goat>cougar": ["a"], "deer>cougar": ["g", "Puma concolor", "Odocoileus hemionus"], "elk>cougar": ["g", "Puma concolor", "Cervus canadensis"], "deer>bear": ["g", "Ursus americanus", "Odocoileus hemionus"], "elk>bear": ["g", "Ursus americanus", "Cervus canadensis"], "vole>bear": ["g", "Ursus americanus", "Myodes gapperi"], "vole>fox": ["g", "Vulpes vulpes", "Myodes gapperi"], "vole>hawk": ["g", "Buteo jamaicensis", "Myodes gapperi"], "deer>fox": ["g", "Vulpes vulpes", "Odocoileus hemionus"], "deer>raven": ["gg", "Corvus corax", "Odocoileus hemionus"], "elk>raven": ["g", "Corvus corax", "Cervus canadensis"], "vole>raven": ["gg", "Corvus corax", "Myodes gapperi"], "hemlock>deer": ["ga", "Odocoileus hemionus", "Tsuga heterophylla"], "goat>bear": ["ga", "Ursus americanus", "Oreamnos americanus"], "deer>hawk": ["ga", "Buteo jamaicensis", "Odocoileus hemionus"], "dsquirrel>raven": ["ga", "Corvus corax", "Tamiasciurus douglasii"], "bear>cougar": ["ga", "Puma concolor", "Ursus americanus"], "fox>cougar": ["ga", "Puma concolor", "Vulpes vulpes"], "goat>goldeneagle": ["ga", "Aquila chrysaetos", "Oreamnos americanus"], "deer>goldeneagle": ["ga", "Aquila chrysaetos", "Odocoileus hemionus"], "elk>goldeneagle": ["ga", "Aquila chrysaetos", "Cervus canadensis"], "fox>goldeneagle": ["ga", "Aquila chrysaetos", "Vulpes vulpes"], "hawk>goldeneagle": ["ga", "Aquila chrysaetos", "Buteo jamaicensis"], "raven>goldeneagle": ["ga", "Aquila chrysaetos", "Corvus corax"]}, "story": "Mount Rainier National Park in Washington protects a 14,406-foot volcano, the highest point in the Cascade Range. Over 25 glaciers descend its flanks, and old-growth forest covers 91,000 acres of the park. It was the fourth national park in the United States, established in 1899.", "matters": "Carbon Glacier is the largest glacier by volume in the contiguous United States. Clouds around the peak drop huge amounts of rain and snow."}